# Example reverse proxy for a SaaS/single-VPS deployment (see
# ../NETWORK_TOPOLOGY.md). Caddy is the only process that binds a public
# interface — it terminates TLS (automatic, via Let's Encrypt) and proxies
# to exactly two things, on separate domains: TrustPay Backend (the
# consumer app's own traffic) and the gateway (external bank/developer API
# traffic, tiered keys, rate limited — services/gateway). Different
# audiences, deliberately kept on different domains rather than one
# proxy routing by path. Ledger, Payments, and Compliance are not
# reachable through this or any other route from outside the box; they
# bind 127.0.0.1 themselves regardless of what's in front of them.

trustpay.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8082
}

api.trustbank.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8084
}

# Nothing else is proxied. Do not add routes for :8080 (Ledger), :8081
# (Payments), or :8083 (Compliance) here — if a future admin/ops tool
# needs to reach them from outside the box, put it behind its own
# authenticated route or a VPN, not this proxy.
